IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa-definitions`
IMPORT `coa20-part26`
IMPORT `coa20-part26a`
IMPORT `coa20-part27-merger`

-- coa20-part27-division.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 27 (Mergers and divisions of public companies), Chapter 3 (Division),
-- ss 919 to 934, lines 12801-13034 of ukpga-2006-46.txt. LAYER 1, objective. Most sections of this Chapter are the twins of sections of Chapter 2
-- (ss 906 to 918A): they are instantiated from the merger module's blocks by work/expand.py (renaming and re-pointing the quotations,
-- checked word by word against the twin's text with work/twin.py), and the passages where the twins differ are written by hand beside them:
-- 920(3) (property, liabilities and allocation), 921(4) and 926(4) (the court's power in s 934), 922(2), 923(3) (the s 593 report),
-- 928, 931(6) (the fourth condition is a report of material change, not a 5% requisition), 931A, 932(5), 933, 933A and 934.
-- Answers are as in coa20-part27-merger.l4: a requirement answers a `s 903(1) status of a requirement`, an exclusion a MAYBE BOOLEAN.


-- ===========================================================================================================
§ `Part 27, Chapter 3 -- Division`
-- ===========================================================================================================

§§ `Divisions and companies involved in a division (s 919)`

-- JURAL none (a definition)
-- src:12804 | (1) The scheme involves a division where under the scheme the undertaking, property and liabilities of the company in respect of which the compromise or arrangement is proposed are to be divided among and transferred to two or more companies each of which is either—
-- src:12805 | (a) an existing public company, or
-- src:12806 | (b) a new company (whether or not a public company).
@ref s 919(1) The scheme involves a division (src:12804-12806)
GIVEN `the undertaking, property and liabilities of the company in respect of which the compromise or arrangement is proposed are to be divided among and transferred to two or more companies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `each of those companies is either an existing public company or a new company (whether or not a public company)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 919(1) the scheme involves a division` MEANS
    IF `the undertaking, property and liabilities of the company in respect of which the compromise or arrangement is proposed are to be divided among and transferred to two or more companies` AND `each of those companies is either an existing public company or a new company (whether or not a public company)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The scheme involves a division where under the scheme the undertaking, property and liabilities of the company ... are to be divided among and transferred to two or more companies each of which is either— (a) an existing public company, or (b) a new company"

-- src:12807 | (2) References in this Part to the companies involved in the division are to the transferor company and any existing transferee companies.
@ref s 919(2) "the companies involved in the division" (src:12807)
GIVEN `the company is the transferor company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is an existing transferee company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 919(2) the company is one of the companies involved in the division` MEANS
    IF `the company is the transferor company` OR `the company is an existing transferee company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "References in this Part to the companies involved in the division are to the transferor company and any existing transferee companies"

§§ `Draft terms of scheme (division) (s 920)`

-- JURAL the members and creditors: claim to draft terms | the directors of each company involved in the division: duty to draw them up and adopt them
-- src:12810 | (1) A draft of the proposed terms of the scheme must be drawn up and adopted by the directors of each of the companies involved in the division.
@ref s 920(1) A draft of the proposed terms must be drawn up and adopted by the directors of each of the companies involved in the division (src:12810)
GIVEN `a draft of the proposed terms of the scheme has been drawn up` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has been adopted by the directors of each of the companies involved in the division` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 903(1) status of a requirement`
`s 920(1) the draft terms have been drawn up and adopted` MEANS
    IF `a draft of the proposed terms of the scheme has been drawn up` AND `it has been adopted by the directors of each of the companies involved in the division`
    THEN `s 903(1) requirement complied with`
    ELSE `s 903(1) requirement not complied with` -- a bare "must" not done (fork F3)

-- Unlike s 905(2)(b) to (d), nothing excludes any of these particulars (s 915 is a merger section).
-- JURAL the members: claim to the particulars | the directors of the companies involved in the division: duty to give them
-- src:12811 | (2) The draft terms must give particulars of at least the following matters—
-- src:12812 | (a) in respect of the transferor company and each transferee company—
-- src:12813 | (i) its name,
-- src:12814 | (ii) the address of its registered office, and
-- src:12815 | (iii) whether it is a company limited by shares or a company limited by guarantee and having a share capital;
-- src:12816 | (b) the number of shares in a transferee company to be allotted to members of the transferor company for a given number of their shares (the “share exchange ratio”) and the amount of any cash payment;
-- src:12817 | (c) the terms relating to the allotment of shares in a transferee company;
-- src:12818 | (d) the date from which the holding of shares in a transferee company will entitle the holders to participate in profits, and any special conditions affecting that entitlement;
-- src:12819 | (e) the date from which the transactions of the transferor company are to be treated for accounting purposes as being those of a transferee company;
-- src:12820 | (f) any rights or restrictions attaching to shares or other securities in a transferee company to be allotted under the scheme to the holders of shares or other securities in the transferor company to which any special rights or restrictions attach, or the measures proposed concerning them;
-- src:12821 | (g) any amount of benefit paid or given or intended to be paid or given—
-- src:12822 | (i) to any of the experts referred to in section 924 (expert's report), or
-- src:12823 | (ii) to any director of a company involved in the division,
-- src:12824 | and the consideration for the payment of benefit.
@ref s 920(2) The draft terms must give particulars of at least the listed matters (src:12811-12824)
GIVEN `the name of the transferor company and of each transferee company is given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the address of the registered office of each is given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `whether each is a company limited by shares or a company limited by guarantee and having a share capital is given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of shares in a transferee company to be allotted to members of the transferor company for a given number of their shares (the share exchange ratio) and the amount of any cash payment are given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the terms relating to the allotment of shares in a transferee company are given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date from which the holding of shares in a transferee company will entitle the holders to participate in profits, and any special conditions affecting that entitlement, are given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date from which the transactions of the transferor company are to be treated for accounting purposes as being those of a transferee company is given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any rights or restrictions attaching to shares or other securities in a transferee company to be allotted to holders of securities with special rights or restrictions, or the measures proposed concerning them, are given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any amount of benefit paid or given or intended to be paid or given to any of the experts or to any director of a company involved in the division, and the consideration for the payment of benefit, are given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 903(1) status of a requirement`
`s 920(2) the draft terms give the particulars required` MEANS
    IF `the name of the transferor company and of each transferee company is given` AND `the address of the registered office of each is given`
       AND `whether each is a company limited by shares or a company limited by guarantee and having a share capital is given`
       AND `the number of shares in a transferee company to be allotted to members of the transferor company for a given number of their shares (the share exchange ratio) and the amount of any cash payment are given`
       AND `the terms relating to the allotment of shares in a transferee company are given`
       AND `the date from which the holding of shares in a transferee company will entitle the holders to participate in profits, and any special conditions affecting that entitlement, are given`
       AND `the date from which the transactions of the transferor company are to be treated for accounting purposes as being those of a transferee company is given`
       AND `any rights or restrictions attaching to shares or other securities in a transferee company to be allotted to holders of securities with special rights or restrictions, or the measures proposed concerning them, are given`
       AND `any amount of benefit paid or given or intended to be paid or given to any of the experts or to any director of a company involved in the division, and the consideration for the payment of benefit, are given`
    THEN `s 903(1) requirement complied with`
    ELSE `s 903(1) requirement not complied with` -- a bare "must ... give particulars of at least" not done (fork F3)

-- src:12825 | (3) The draft terms must also—
-- src:12826 | (a) give particulars of the property and liabilities to be transferred (to the extent that these are known to the transferor company) and their allocation among the transferee companies;
-- src:12827 | (b) make provision for the allocation among and transfer to the transferee companies of any other property and liabilities that the transferor company has acquired or may subsequently acquire; and
-- src:12828 | (c) specify the allocation to members of the transferor company of shares in the transferee companies and the criteria upon which that allocation is based.
@ref s 920(3) The draft terms must also give particulars of the property and liabilities, provide for the allocation of other property and liabilities, and specify the allocation of shares to members (src:12825-12828)
GIVEN `the draft terms give particulars of the property and liabilities to be transferred (to the extent that these are known to the transferor company) and their allocation among the transferee companies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the draft terms make provision for the allocation among and transfer to the transferee companies of any other property and liabilities that the transferor company has acquired or may subsequently acquire` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the draft terms specify the allocation to members of the transferor company of shares in the transferee companies and the criteria upon which that allocation is based` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 903(1) status of a requirement`
`s 920(3) the draft terms also do what the section requires` MEANS
    IF `the draft terms give particulars of the property and liabilities to be transferred (to the extent that these are known to the transferor company) and their allocation among the transferee companies`
       AND `the draft terms make provision for the allocation among and transfer to the transferee companies of any other property and liabilities that the transferor company has acquired or may subsequently acquire`
       AND `the draft terms specify the allocation to members of the transferor company of shares in the transferee companies and the criteria upon which that allocation is based`
    THEN `s 903(1) requirement complied with`
    ELSE `s 903(1) requirement not complied with` -- a bare "must also" not done (fork F3)

§§ `Publication of draft terms by registrar (division) (s 921)`

-- (instantiated from the twin block of Publication of draft terms by registrar (merger) (s 906); see work/expand.py)
§§ `Publication of draft terms by registrar (division) (s 921)`

-- JURAL the registrar (receipt of the draft terms): none | the directors of each company involved in the division: duty to deliver a copy
-- src:12830 | (1) The directors of each company involved in the division must deliver a copy of the draft terms to the registrar.
@ref s 921(1) The directors of each company involved in the division must deliver a copy of the draft terms to the registrar (src:12830)
GIVEN `s 921(4) the requirements in section 921 are excluded` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the directors of the company have delivered a copy of the draft terms to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 903(1) status of a requirement`
`s 921(1) the directors have delivered a copy of the draft terms to the registrar` MEANS
    `s 903(1) the status of the requirement` `s 921(4) the requirements in section 921 are excluded` `the directors of the company have delivered a copy of the draft terms to the registrar`

-- JURAL the members and creditors: claim to publication of notice of receipt | the registrar: duty to publish (an official: no seat)
-- src:12831 | (2) The registrar must publish in the Gazette notice of receipt by him from that company of a copy of the draft terms.
@ref s 921(2) The registrar must publish in the Gazette notice of receipt of a copy of the draft terms (src:12831)
GIVEN `the registrar has received from the company a copy of the draft terms` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the registrar has published notice of receipt in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 921(2) the registrar has published notice of receipt of the draft terms in the Gazette` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the registrar has received from the company a copy of the draft terms`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "notice of receipt by him from that company of a copy of the draft terms" (no copy received)
    ELSE IF `the registrar has published notice of receipt in the Gazette`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The registrar must publish in the Gazette notice of receipt" (a bare "must" not done: fork F3)

-- "at least one month before the date of any meeting": the notice date plus one calendar month is on or before the meeting date. No meeting summoned: not covered.
-- src:12832 | (3) That notice must be published at least one month before the date of any meeting of that company summoned for the purposes of approving the scheme.
@ref s 921(3) The notice must be published at least one month before the date of any meeting summoned to approve the scheme (src:12832)
GIVEN `date the notice was published in the Gazette` IS A DATE
      `date of the first meeting of the company summoned for the purpose of approving the scheme` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 921(3) the notice was published at least one month before the meeting` MEANS
    CONSIDER `date of the first meeting of the company summoned for the purpose of approving the scheme`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "before the date of any meeting of that company summoned for the purpose of approving the scheme" (no meeting is summoned)
    WHEN JUST meeting THEN
        IF `s 906(3) the date one month before` meeting AT LEAST `date the notice was published in the Gazette`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be published at least one month before the date of any meeting"

-- JURAL none (a signpost whose effect is ss 921A and 934)
-- src:12833 | (4) The requirements in this section are subject to section 921A (publication of draft terms on company website) and section 934 (power of court to exclude certain requirements).
@ref s 921(4) The requirements in this section are subject to sections 921A and 934 (src:12833)
GIVEN `s 921A(1) section 921 does not apply in respect of the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 934(1)(a) the court has directed that sections 921 and 926 do not apply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 921(4) the requirements in section 921 are excluded` MEANS
    `s 903(2) any of the provisions answers yes` (LIST `s 921A(1) section 921 does not apply in respect of the company`, `s 934(1)(a) the court has directed that sections 921 and 926 do not apply`)

§§ `Publication of draft terms on company website (division) (s 921A)`

-- (instantiated from the twin block of Publication of draft terms on company website (merger) (s 906A); see work/expand.py)
§§ `Publication of draft terms on company website (division) (s 921A)`

-- The first condition: the draft terms are on a website maintained by or on behalf of the company, which identifies it.
-- src:12836 | (2) The first condition is that the draft terms are made available on a website which—
-- src:12837 | (a) is maintained by or on behalf of the company, and
-- src:12838 | (b) identifies the company.
@ref s 921A(2) The first condition: the draft terms are on the company's website (src:12836-12838)
GIVEN `the draft terms are made available on a website` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the website is maintained by or on behalf of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the website identifies the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 921A(2) the first condition is met` MEANS
    IF `the draft terms are made available on a website` AND `the website is maintained by or on behalf of the company` AND `the website identifies the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The first condition is that the draft terms are made available on a website which— (a) is maintained by or on behalf of the company, and (b) identifies the company"

-- src:12839 | (3) The second condition is that neither access to the draft terms on the website nor the supply of a hard copy of them from the website is conditional on payment of a fee or otherwise restricted.
@ref s 921A(3) The second condition: access and the supply of a hard copy are not conditional on a fee or otherwise restricted (src:12839)
GIVEN `access to the draft terms on the website is conditional on payment of a fee or otherwise restricted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the supply of a hard copy of them from the website is conditional on payment of a fee or otherwise restricted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 921A(3) the second condition is met` MEANS
    IF NOT (`access to the draft terms on the website is conditional on payment of a fee or otherwise restricted` OR `the supply of a hard copy of them from the website is conditional on payment of a fee or otherwise restricted`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The second condition is that neither access to the draft terms on the website nor the supply of a hard copy of them from the website is conditional on payment of a fee or otherwise restricted"

-- src:12840 | (4) The third condition is that the directors of the company deliver to the registrar a notice giving details of the website.
@ref s 921A(4) The third condition: the directors deliver to the registrar a notice giving details of the website (src:12840)
GIVEN `the directors of the company have delivered to the registrar a notice giving details of the website` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 921A(4) the third condition is met` MEANS
    IF `the directors of the company have delivered to the registrar a notice giving details of the website`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The third condition is that the directors of the company deliver to the registrar a notice giving details of the website"

-- src:12841 | (5) The fourth condition is that the registrar publishes the notice in the Gazette at least one month before the date of any meeting of the company summoned for the purpose of approving the scheme.
@ref s 921A(5) The fourth condition: the registrar publishes the notice in the Gazette at least one month before the meeting (src:12841)
GIVEN `date the registrar published the notice in the Gazette` IS A DATE
      `date of the first meeting of the company summoned for the purpose of approving the scheme` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 921A(5) the fourth condition is met` MEANS
    IF `s 906(3) the date one month before` `date of the first meeting of the company summoned for the purpose of approving the scheme` AT LEAST `date the registrar published the notice in the Gazette`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The fourth condition is that the registrar publishes the notice in the Gazette at least one month before the date of any meeting"

-- The fifth condition: available throughout the period [one month before the meeting, the meeting], unless s 940A disregards the failure.
-- src:12842 | (6) The fifth condition is that the draft terms remain available on the website throughout the period beginning one month before, and ending on, the date of any such meeting.
@ref s 921A(6) The fifth condition: the draft terms remain available on the website throughout the period (src:12842)
GIVEN `first day of continuous availability` IS A DATE
      `last day of continuous availability` IS A DATE
      `date of the first meeting of the company summoned for the purpose of approving the scheme` IS A DATE
      `s 940A(1) the failure to make the draft terms available throughout the period is to be disregarded` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 921A(6) the fifth condition is met` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 906A(6) the document was available throughout the period beginning one month before, and ending on, the date` `first day of continuous availability` `last day of continuous availability` `date of the first meeting of the company summoned for the purpose of approving the scheme`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 940A(1) the failure to make the draft terms available throughout the period is to be disregarded` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE -- s 940A: the failure "is to be disregarded"
        IF `s 940A(1) the failure to make the draft terms available throughout the period is to be disregarded` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether section 940A disregards the failure is not known
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The fifth condition is that the draft terms remain available on the website throughout the period beginning one month before, and ending on, the date of any such meeting"

-- JURAL the company: immunity from section 921 | the registrar: disability to require delivery and publication
-- src:12835 | (1) Section 921 does not apply in respect of a company if the conditions in subsections (2) to (6) are met.
@ref s 921A(1) Section 921 does not apply in respect of a company if the conditions in subsections (2) to (6) are met (src:12835)
GIVEN `s 921A(2) the first condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 921A(3) the second condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 921A(4) the third condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 921A(5) the fourth condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 921A(6) the fifth condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 921A(1) section 921 does not apply in respect of the company` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF elem (JUST FALSE) (LIST `s 921A(2) the first condition is met`, `s 921A(3) the second condition is met`, `s 921A(4) the third condition is met`, `s 921A(5) the fourth condition is met`, `s 921A(6) the fifth condition is met`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Section 921 does not apply in respect of a company if the conditions in subsections (2) to (6) are met" (an unmet "if": marginal reading (a))
        IF elem NOTHING (LIST `s 921A(2) the first condition is met`, `s 921A(3) the second condition is met`, `s 921A(4) the third condition is met`, `s 921A(5) the fourth condition is met`, `s 921A(6) the fifth condition is met`)
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a condition's answer is not known and none has failed
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `Approval of members of companies involved in the division (s 922)`

-- (instantiated from the twin block of Approval of members of merging companies (s 907); see work/expand.py)
§§ `Approval of members of companies involved in the division (s 922)`

-- One class of members at a meeting: the number present and voting, the number for, and the value present and voting and for.
DECLARE `s 922(1) votes of a class of members` HAS
    `s 922(1) number present and voting` IS A NUMBER
    `s 922(1) number for the scheme` IS A NUMBER
    `s 922(1) value present and voting` IS A NUMBER
    `s 922(1) value for the scheme` IS A NUMBER

-- A majority in number (more than half) representing 75% in value (at least 75%), present and voting in person or by proxy; every class of each merging company.
-- JURAL the members of each merging company: right to vote on the scheme | the directors and the company: duty to put it to them; the scheme: no effect without the approval
-- src:12844 | (1) The scheme must be approved by a majority in number, representing 75% in value, of each class of members of each of the companies involved in the division, present and voting either in person or by proxy at a meeting.
@ref s 922(1) The scheme must be approved by a majority in number, representing 75% in value, of each class of members of each of the companies involved in the division (src:12844)
GIVEN `s 922(2) the meeting of members is not required` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      classes IS A LIST OF `s 922(1) votes of a class of members`
GIVETH A `s 903(1) status of a requirement`
`s 922(1) the scheme has been approved by the members of a company involved in the division` MEANS
    `s 903(1) the status of the requirement` `s 922(2) the meeting of members is not required`
        (all (GIVEN class YIELD 2 TIMES class's `s 922(1) number for the scheme` GREATER THAN class's `s 922(1) number present and voting`
                                AND class's `s 922(1) value for the scheme` AT LEAST (0.75 TIMES class's `s 922(1) value present and voting`)) classes)

-- src:12845 | (2) This requirement is subject to sections 931, 931A and 932 (circumstances in which meeting of members not required).
@ref s 922(2) The requirement is subject to sections 931, 931A and 932 (src:12845)
GIVEN `s 931(2) the meeting of members of the transferor company is not required` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 931A(1) the meeting of members of the transferor company is not required` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 932(1) the meeting of members of the transferee company is not required` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 922(2) the meeting of members is not required` MEANS
    `s 903(2) any of the provisions answers yes` (LIST `s 931(2) the meeting of members of the transferor company is not required`, `s 931A(1) the meeting of members of the transferor company is not required`, `s 932(1) the meeting of members of the transferee company is not required`)

§§ `Directors' explanatory report (division) (s 923)`

-- (instantiated from the twin block of Directors' explanatory report (merger) (s 908); see work/expand.py)
§§ `Directors' explanatory report (division) (s 923)`

-- JURAL the members: claim to the report | the directors of each merging company: duty to draw it up and adopt it
-- src:12847 | (1) The directors of the transferor and each existing transferee company must draw up and adopt a report.
@ref s 923(1) The directors of each merging company must draw up and adopt a report (src:12847)
GIVEN `s 923(4) the requirement in section 923 is excluded` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the directors of the company have drawn up and adopted a report` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 903(1) status of a requirement`
`s 923(1) the directors have drawn up and adopted a report` MEANS
    `s 903(1) the status of the requirement` `s 923(4) the requirement in section 923 is excluded` `the directors of the company have drawn up and adopted a report`

-- (2)(b): "insofar as that statement does not deal with the following matters, a further statement": the grounds and the valuation difficulties may be in either.
-- src:12848 | (2) The report must consist of—
-- src:12849 | (a) the required statement explaining the effect of the compromise or arrangement, and
-- src:12850 | (b) insofar as that statement does not deal with the following matters, a further statement—
-- src:12851 | (i) setting out the legal and economic grounds for the draft terms, and in particular for the share exchange ratio and for the criteria on which the allocation to the members of the transferor company of shares in the transferee companies was based, and
-- src:12852 | (ii) specifying any special valuation difficulties.
@ref s 923(2) The report must consist of the required statement and, insofar as it does not deal with them, a further statement (src:12848-12852)
GIVEN `the report includes the required statement explaining the effect of the compromise or arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the required statement sets out the legal and economic grounds for the draft terms, and in particular for the share exchange ratio` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the required statement specifies any special valuation difficulties` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a further statement sets out the legal and economic grounds for the draft terms, and in particular for the share exchange ratio` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a further statement specifies any special valuation difficulties` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 923(2) the report consists of what the section requires` MEANS
    IF `the report includes the required statement explaining the effect of the compromise or arrangement`
       AND (`the required statement sets out the legal and economic grounds for the draft terms, and in particular for the share exchange ratio` OR `a further statement sets out the legal and economic grounds for the draft terms, and in particular for the share exchange ratio`)
       AND (`the required statement specifies any special valuation difficulties` OR `a further statement specifies any special valuation difficulties`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The report must consist of— (a) the required statement ..., and (b) insofar as that statement does not deal with the following matters, a further statement" (a bare "must" not done: fork F3)

DECLARE `s 923(2A) the statement required` IS ONE OF
    `s 923(2A)(a) the statement required by section 897`
    `s 923(2A)(b) the statement required by section 901D`

-- src:12853 | (2A) In subsection (2) “the required statement explaining the effect of the compromise or arrangement” means—
-- src:12854 | (a) in a case where a meeting is summoned under section 896 in relation to the compromise or arrangement, the statement required by section 897;
-- src:12855 | (b) in a case where a meeting is summoned under section 901C in relation to the compromise or arrangement, the statement required by section 901D.
@ref s 923(2A) "the required statement explaining the effect of the compromise or arrangement" (src:12853-12855)
GIVEN `a meeting is summoned under section 896 in relation to the compromise or arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a meeting is summoned under section 901C in relation to the compromise or arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 923(2A) the statement required`
`s 923(2A) the required statement explaining the effect of the compromise or arrangement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a meeting is summoned under section 896 in relation to the compromise or arrangement` AND NOT (`a meeting is summoned under section 901C in relation to the compromise or arrangement`)
            THEN JUST `s 923(2A)(a) the statement required by section 897`
        IF `a meeting is summoned under section 901C in relation to the compromise or arrangement` AND NOT (`a meeting is summoned under section 896 in relation to the compromise or arrangement`)
            THEN JUST `s 923(2A)(b) the statement required by section 901D`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in a case where a meeting is summoned under section 896 ...; in a case where a meeting is summoned under section 901C": neither, or both, is said to be the case

-- JURAL the members: claim to a statement whether a section 593 valuation report was made and delivered | the directors: duty to state it
-- src:12856 | (3) The report must also state—
-- src:12857 | (a) whether a report has been made to any transferee company under section 593 (valuation of non-cash consideration for shares), and
-- src:12858 | (b) if so, whether that report has been delivered to the registrar of companies.
@ref s 923(3) The report must also state whether a report has been made under section 593 and whether it has been delivered to the registrar (src:12856-12858)
GIVEN `the report states whether a report has been made to any transferee company under section 593 (valuation of non-cash consideration for shares)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a report has been made to a transferee company under section 593` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report states whether that report has been delivered to the registrar of companies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 923(3) the report states what the section requires` MEANS
    IF `the report states whether a report has been made to any transferee company under section 593 (valuation of non-cash consideration for shares)`
       AND ((NOT (`a report has been made to a transferee company under section 593`)) OR `the report states whether that report has been delivered to the registrar of companies`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The report must also state— (a) whether a report has been made to any transferee company under section 593 ..., and (b) if so, whether that report has been delivered to the registrar of companies" (a bare "must" not done: fork F3)

-- src:12859 | (4) The requirement in this section is subject to section 933 (agreement to dispense with reports etc) and section 933A (certain requirements excluded where shareholders given proportional rights).
@ref s 923(4) The requirement is subject to sections 933 and 933A (src:12859)
GIVEN `s 933(1) the requirements are dispensed with by agreement` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 933A(2) the requirements of sections 923, 924, 925 and 927 do not apply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 923(4) the requirement in section 923 is excluded` MEANS
    `s 903(2) any of the provisions answers yes` (LIST `s 933(1) the requirements are dispensed with by agreement`, `s 933A(2) the requirements of sections 923, 924, 925 and 927 do not apply`)

§§ `Expert's report (division) (s 924)`

-- (instantiated from the twin block of Expert's report (merger) (s 909); see work/expand.py)
§§ `Expert's report (division) (s 924)`

-- JURAL the members: claim to an expert's report | each company involved in the division: duty to have one drawn up
-- src:12861 | (1) An expert's report must be drawn up on behalf of each company involved in the division.
-- src:12862 | (2) The report required is a written report on the draft terms to the members of the company.
@ref s 924(1) An expert's report must be drawn up on behalf of each company involved in the division: a written report on the draft terms to the members (src:12861-12862)
GIVEN `s 924(7) the requirement in section 924 is excluded` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a written report on the draft terms to the members of the company has been drawn up on its behalf by an expert` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 903(1) status of a requirement`
`s 924(1) an expert's report has been drawn up on behalf of the company` MEANS
    `s 903(1) the status of the requirement` `s 924(7) the requirement in section 924 is excluded` `a written report on the draft terms to the members of the company has been drawn up on its behalf by an expert`

-- JURAL the companies involved in the division (jointly): power to apply for a joint expert | the court: liability to hear it
-- src:12863 | (3) The court may on the joint application of the companies involved in the division approve the appointment of a joint expert to draw up a single report on behalf of all those companies.
-- src:12864 | If no such appointment is made, there must be a separate expert's report to the members of each company involved in the division drawn up by a separate expert appointed on behalf of that company.
@ref s 924(3) The court may on the joint application of the companies involved in the division approve a joint expert; otherwise a separate expert for each (src:12863-12864)
GIVEN `the court has approved the appointment of a joint expert on the joint application of the companies involved in the division` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a single report has been drawn up by the joint expert on behalf of the companies involved in the division` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a separate expert's report to the members of each company involved in the division has been drawn up by a separate expert appointed on behalf of that company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 924(3) the way the expert's report is drawn up complies` MEANS
    IF `the court has approved the appointment of a joint expert on the joint application of the companies involved in the division`
    THEN (IF `a single report has been drawn up by the joint expert on behalf of the companies involved in the division`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING) -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text allows the court's approval of a joint expert and does not say a separate report is then forbidden
    ELSE (IF `a separate expert's report to the members of each company involved in the division has been drawn up by a separate expert appointed on behalf of that company`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE) -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If no such appointment is made, there must be a separate expert's report to the members of each company involved in the division drawn up by a separate expert"

-- JURAL none (a rule fixing who may be the expert)
-- src:12865 | (4) The expert must be a person who—
-- src:12866 | (a) is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor (see section 1212), and
-- src:12867 | (b) meets the independence requirement in section 936.
@ref s 924(4) The expert must be eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor and meet the independence requirement (src:12865-12867)
GIVEN `s 1212 the person is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 936(1) the person meets the independence requirement` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 924(4) the person may be the expert` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 1212 the person is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `s 936(1) the person meets the independence requirement` EQUALS JUST FALSE
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The expert must be a person who— (a) is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor ..., and (b) meets the independence requirement in section 936"
        IF `s 1212 the person is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `s 936(1) the person meets the independence requirement` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): section 1212 or section 936 is not answered

-- (e) applies only to a valuation made by a person other than the expert (section 935).
-- src:12868 | (5) The expert's report must—
-- src:12869 | (a) indicate the method or methods used to arrive at the share exchange ratio;
-- src:12870 | (b) give an opinion as to whether the method or methods used are reasonable in all the circumstances of the case, indicate the values arrived at using each such method and (if there is more than one method) give an opinion on the relative importance attributed to such methods in arriving at the value decided on;
-- src:12871 | (c) describe any special valuation difficulties that have arisen;
-- src:12872 | (d) state whether in the expert's opinion the share exchange ratio is reasonable; and
-- src:12873 | (e) in the case of a valuation made by a person other than himself (see section 935), state that it appeared to him reasonable to arrange for it to be so made or to accept a valuation so made.
@ref s 924(5) What the expert's report must contain (src:12868-12873)
GIVEN `the report indicates the method or methods used to arrive at the share exchange ratio` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report gives an opinion on whether the method or methods used are reasonable, indicates the values arrived at using each method and, if there is more than one, gives an opinion on their relative importance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report describes any special valuation difficulties that have arisen` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report states whether in the expert's opinion the share exchange ratio is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a valuation was made by a person other than the expert` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report states that it appeared to the expert reasonable to arrange for it to be so made or to accept a valuation so made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 924(5) the expert's report contains what the section requires` MEANS
    IF `the report indicates the method or methods used to arrive at the share exchange ratio`
       AND `the report gives an opinion on whether the method or methods used are reasonable, indicates the values arrived at using each method and, if there is more than one, gives an opinion on their relative importance`
       AND `the report describes any special valuation difficulties that have arisen`
       AND `the report states whether in the expert's opinion the share exchange ratio is reasonable`
       AND ((NOT (`a valuation was made by a person other than the expert`)) OR `the report states that it appeared to the expert reasonable to arrange for it to be so made or to accept a valuation so made`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The expert's report must— (a) indicate the method or methods ...; (e) in the case of a valuation made by a person other than himself ..., state that it appeared to him reasonable" (a bare "must" not done: fork F3)

-- JURAL the expert: claim of access to documents and to information from the officers | the companies involved in the division and their officers: duty to give them
-- src:12874 | (6) The expert (or each of them) has—
-- src:12875 | (a) the right of access to all such documents of the companies involved in the division, and
-- src:12876 | (b) the right to require from the companies' officers all such information,
-- src:12877 | as he thinks necessary for the purposes of making his report.
@ref s 924(6) The expert has a right of access to documents and to require information from the officers (src:12874-12877)
GIVEN `the person is the expert (or one of the experts)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the expert thinks the document or information necessary for the purposes of making his report` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 924(6) the expert has the right of access to the document or to require the information` MEANS
    IF `the person is the expert (or one of the experts)` AND `the expert thinks the document or information necessary for the purposes of making his report`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The expert (or each of them) has ... all such documents ... as he thinks necessary for the purposes of making his report"

-- src:12878 | (7) The requirement in this section is subject to section 933 (agreement to dispense with reports etc) and section 933A (certain requirements excluded where shareholders given proportional rights).
@ref s 924(7) The requirement is subject to sections 933 and 933A (src:12878)
GIVEN `s 933(1) the requirements are dispensed with by agreement` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 933A(2) the requirements of sections 923, 924, 925 and 927 do not apply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 924(7) the requirement in section 924 is excluded` MEANS
    `s 903(2) any of the provisions answers yes` (LIST `s 933(1) the requirements are dispensed with by agreement`, `s 933A(2) the requirements of sections 923, 924, 925 and 927 do not apply`)

§§ `Supplementary accounting statement (division) (s 925)`

-- (instantiated from the twin block of Supplementary accounting statement (merger) (s 910); see work/expand.py)
§§ `Supplementary accounting statement (division) (s 925)`

-- (1)(a): the last annual accounts relate to a financial year that ended before the date seven months before the first meeting; (b) if no meeting is
-- required (ss 916 to 918): before the date six months before the directors adopt the draft terms. NOTHING for the meeting date means no meeting is required.
-- src:12880 | (1) This section applies if the last annual accounts of a company involved in the division relate to a financial year ending before—
-- src:12881 | (a) the date seven months before the first meeting of the company summoned for the purposes of approving the scheme, or
-- src:12882 | (b) if no meeting of the company is required (by virtue of section 931, 931A or 932), the date six months before the directors of the company adopt the draft terms of the scheme.
@ref s 925(1) The section applies if the last annual accounts relate to a financial year ending too long before (src:12880-12882)
GIVEN `the end of the financial year to which the last annual accounts relate` IS A DATE
      `date of the first meeting of the company summoned for the purposes of approving the scheme` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `date the directors of the company adopt the draft terms of the scheme` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 925(1) this section applies` MEANS
    CONSIDER `date of the first meeting of the company summoned for the purposes of approving the scheme`
    WHEN JUST meeting THEN
        IF `the end of the financial year to which the last annual accounts relate` LESS THAN (`s 910(1) the date a number of months before` meeting 7)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies if the last annual accounts of a company involved in the division relate to a financial year ending before— (a) the date seven months before the first meeting"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF `the end of the financial year to which the last annual accounts relate` LESS THAN (`s 910(1) the date a number of months before` `date the directors of the company adopt the draft terms of the scheme` 6)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) if no meeting of the company is required (by virtue of any of section 931, 931A or 932), the date six months before the directors of the company adopt the draft terms of the scheme"

-- JURAL the members: claim to a supplementary accounting statement | the directors: duty to prepare it
-- src:12883 | (1A) If the company has not made public a half-yearly financial report relating to a period ending on or after the date mentioned in subsection (1), the directors of the company must prepare a supplementary accounting statement.
@ref s 925(1A) If the company has not made public a half-yearly financial report for a period ending on or after that date, the directors must prepare a statement (src:12883)
GIVEN `s 925(1) this section applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 925(5) the requirement in section 925 is excluded` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company has made public a half-yearly financial report relating to a period ending on or after the date mentioned in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors of the company have prepared a supplementary accounting statement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 903(1) status of a requirement`
`s 925(1A) the directors have prepared a supplementary accounting statement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 925(1) this section applies` EQUALS NOTHING THEN `s 903(1) requirement not covered` -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the section applies is not known
        IF `s 925(1) this section applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN `s 903(1) requirement does not apply` -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies if"
        IF `the company has made public a half-yearly financial report relating to a period ending on or after the date mentioned in subsection (1)` THEN `s 903(1) requirement does not apply` -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the company has not made public a half-yearly financial report"
        OTHERWISE `s 903(1) the status of the requirement` `s 925(5) the requirement in section 925 is excluded` `the directors of the company have prepared a supplementary accounting statement`

-- (2)(a): a balance sheet as at a date not more than three months before the draft terms were adopted. A date after the adoption is not covered by the text.
-- src:12884 | (2) That statement must consist of—
-- src:12885 | (a) a balance sheet dealing with the state of affairs of the company as at a date not more than three months before the draft terms were adopted by the directors, and
-- src:12886 | (b) where the company would be required under section 399 to prepare group accounts if that date were the last day of a financial year, a consolidated balance sheet dealing with the state of affairs of the company and the undertakings that would be included in such a consolidation.
@ref s 925(2) The statement must consist of a balance sheet and, where group accounts would be required, a consolidated balance sheet (src:12884-12886)
GIVEN `the date as at which the balance sheet deals with the state of affairs of the company` IS A DATE
      `date the draft terms were adopted by the directors` IS A DATE
      `s 399 the company would be required to prepare group accounts if that date were the last day of a financial year` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the statement includes a consolidated balance sheet dealing with the state of affairs of the company and the undertakings that would be included in such a consolidation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 925(2) the statement consists of what the section requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the date as at which the balance sheet deals with the state of affairs of the company` GREATER THAN `date the draft terms were adopted by the directors`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text speaks of a date "not more than three months before the draft terms were adopted", not of a later date
        IF `the date as at which the balance sheet deals with the state of affairs of the company` LESS THAN (`s 910(1) the date a number of months before` `date the draft terms were adopted by the directors` 3)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a balance sheet dealing with the state of affairs of the company as at a date not more than three months before the draft terms were adopted"
        IF `s 399 the company would be required to prepare group accounts if that date were the last day of a financial year` EQUALS NOTHING
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): section 399 (group accounts) is outside this range
        IF `s 399 the company would be required to prepare group accounts if that date were the last day of a financial year` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND NOT (`the statement includes a consolidated balance sheet dealing with the state of affairs of the company and the undertakings that would be included in such a consolidation`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) where the company would be required under section 399 to prepare group accounts ..., a consolidated balance sheet"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:12887 | (3) The requirements of this Act ... as to the balance sheet forming part of a company's annual accounts, and the matters to be included in notes to it, apply to the balance sheet required for an accounting statement under this section, with such modifications as are necessary by reason of its being prepared otherwise than as at the last day of a financial year.
@ref s 925(3) The requirements as to the balance sheet of annual accounts apply to this balance sheet with the necessary modifications (src:12887)
GIVEN `the balance sheet is the one required for an accounting statement under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 925(3) the requirements as to the balance sheet of annual accounts apply to the balance sheet` MEANS
    IF `the balance sheet is the one required for an accounting statement under this section` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "apply to the balance sheet required for an accounting statement under this section"

-- src:12888 | (4) The provisions of section 414 as to the approval and signing of accounts apply to the balance sheet required for an accounting statement under this section.
@ref s 925(4) Section 414 (approval and signing of accounts) applies to the balance sheet (src:12888)
GIVEN `the balance sheet is the one required for an accounting statement under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 414 the balance sheet has been approved and signed as that section provides` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 925(4) the balance sheet has been approved and signed as section 414 provides` MEANS
    IF `the balance sheet is the one required for an accounting statement under this section` THEN `s 414 the balance sheet has been approved and signed as that section provides`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "apply to the balance sheet required for an accounting statement under this section"

-- src:12889 | (4A) In this section “ half-yearly financial report ” means a report of that description required to be made public by rules under section 89A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (transparency rules).
@ref s 925(4A) "half-yearly financial report" (src:12889)
GIVEN `the report is of a description required to be made public by rules under section 89A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (transparency rules)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 925(4A) the report is a half-yearly financial report` MEANS
    `the report is of a description required to be made public by rules under section 89A of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (transparency rules)` -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): section 89A of the 2000 Act is not among the sources; the borrowed answer is supplied

-- src:12890 | (5) The requirement in this section is subject to section 933 (agreement to dispense with reports etc) and section 933A (certain requirements excluded where shareholders given proportional rights).
@ref s 925(5) The requirement is subject to sections 933 and 933A (src:12890)
GIVEN `s 933(1) the requirements are dispensed with by agreement` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 933A(2) the requirements of sections 923, 924, 925 and 927 do not apply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 925(5) the requirement in section 925 is excluded` MEANS
