-- JURAL the member (who consented to electronic communication): immunity from the right to hard copy | the company: disability under section 1145
-- src:12908 | (5) Section 1145 (right to hard copy) does not apply to a document sent or supplied in accordance with subsection (1)(b) to a member who has consented to information being sent or supplied by the company by electronic means and has not revoked that consent.
@ref s 926(5) Section 1145 (right to hard copy) does not apply to a document supplied under subsection (1)(b) to a member who has consented to electronic means (src:12908)
GIVEN `the document is sent or supplied in accordance with subsection (1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member has consented to information being sent or supplied by the company by electronic means` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member has not revoked that consent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 926(5) section 1145 does not apply to the document` MEANS
    IF `the document is sent or supplied in accordance with subsection (1)(b)` AND `the member has consented to information being sent or supplied by the company by electronic means` AND `the member has not revoked that consent`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "does not apply to a document sent or supplied in accordance with subsection (1)(b) to a member who has consented ... and has not revoked that consent"

-- src:12909 | (6) Part 4 of Schedule 5 (communications by means of a website) does not apply for the purposes of subsection (1)(b) (but see section 926A(5)).
@ref s 926(6) Part 4 of Schedule 5 (communications by means of a website) does not apply for the purposes of subsection (1)(b) (src:12909)
GIVEN `the purpose is that of subsection (1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 926(6) Part 4 of Schedule 5 does not apply` MEANS
    IF `the purpose is that of subsection (1)(b)` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "does not apply for the purposes of subsection (1)(b) (but see section 926A(5))"

DECLARE `s 926(3) document the members must be able to inspect` IS ONE OF
    `s 926(3)(a) the draft terms`
    `s 926(3)(b) the directors' explanatory report`
    `s 926(3)(c) the expert's report`
    `s 926(3)(d) the company's annual accounts and reports for the last three financial years ending on or before the first meeting`
    `s 926(3)(e) any supplementary accounting statement required by section 925`
    `s 926(3)(f) a recent half-yearly financial report made public instead of the statement`

-- (3)(e) is a document only if section 925 requires a statement; (3)(f) only where no statement is required because a half-yearly report was made public.
-- Subsection (4): the requirements of (3)(b), (c) and (e) are subject to sections 933, 933A and 934, so those documents drop out where `s 926(4)` says so.
-- src:12899 | (3) The documents referred to above are—
-- src:12900 | (a) the draft terms;
-- src:12901 | (b) the directors' explanatory report;
-- src:12902 | (c) the expert's report;
-- src:12903 | (d) the company's annual accounts and reports for the last three financial years ending on or before the first meeting of the members, or any class of members, of the company summoned for the purposes of approving the scheme; . . .
-- src:12904 | (e) any supplementary accounting statement required by section 925; and
-- src:12905 | (f) if no statement is required by section 925 because the company has made public a recent half-yearly financial report (see subsection (1A) of that section), that report.
@ref s 926(3) The documents (src:12899-12905)
GIVEN document IS A `s 926(3) document the members must be able to inspect`
      `s 926(4) the requirements of subsection (3)(b), (c) and (e) are excluded` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a supplementary accounting statement is required by section 925` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no statement is required by section 925 because the company has made public a recent half-yearly financial report` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 926(3) the document is one the members must be able to inspect` MEANS
    CONSIDER document
    WHEN `s 926(3)(a) the draft terms` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 926(3)(b) the directors' explanatory report` THEN
        CONSIDER `s 926(4) the requirements of subsection (3)(b), (c) and (e) are excluded`
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The requirements in subsection (3)(b), (c) and (e) are subject to section 933 ..., section 933A ... and section 934" (the exclusion applies)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether section 933, 933A or 934 excludes the document is not known
    WHEN `s 926(3)(c) the expert's report` THEN
        CONSIDER `s 926(4) the requirements of subsection (3)(b), (c) and (e) are excluded`
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The requirements in subsection (3)(b), (c) and (e) are subject to section 933 ..., section 933A ... and section 934" (the exclusion applies)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether section 933, 933A or 934 excludes the document is not known
    WHEN `s 926(3)(d) the company's annual accounts and reports for the last three financial years ending on or before the first meeting` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 926(3)(e) any supplementary accounting statement required by section 925` THEN
        IF NOT (`a supplementary accounting statement is required by section 925`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any supplementary accounting statement required by section 925"
        ELSE CONSIDER `s 926(4) the requirements of subsection (3)(b), (c) and (e) are excluded`
             WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
             WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The requirements in subsection (3)(b), (c) and (e) are subject to section 933 ..., section 933A ... and section 934" (the exclusion applies)
             WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether section 933, 933A or 934 excludes the document is not known
    WHEN `s 926(3)(f) a recent half-yearly financial report made public instead of the statement` THEN
        IF `no statement is required by section 925 because the company has made public a recent half-yearly financial report` THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if no statement is required by section 925 because the company has made public a recent half-yearly financial report"

-- src:12907 | (4) The requirements in subsection (3)(b), (c) and (e) are subject to section 933 (agreement to dispense with reports etc) , section 933A (certain requirements excluded where shareholders given proportional rights) and section 934 (power of court to exclude certain requirements).
@ref s 926(4) The requirements in subsection (3)(b), (c) and (e) are subject to sections 933, 933A and 934 (src:12907)
GIVEN `s 933(1) the requirements are dispensed with by agreement` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 933A(2) the requirements of sections 923, 924, 925 and 927 do not apply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 934(1)(a) the court has directed that sections 921 and 926 do not apply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 926(4) the requirements of subsection (3)(b), (c) and (e) are excluded` MEANS
    `s 903(2) any of the provisions answers yes` (LIST `s 933(1) the requirements are dispensed with by agreement`, `s 933A(2) the requirements of sections 923, 924, 925 and 927 do not apply`, `s 934(1)(a) the court has directed that sections 921 and 926 do not apply`)

