§§ `Publication of documents on company website (division) (s 926A)`

-- src:12912 | (2) The first condition is that the document is made available on a website which—
-- src:12913 | (a) is maintained by or on behalf of the company, and
-- src:12914 | (b) identifies the company.
@ref s 926A(2) The first condition: the document is on the company's website (src:12912-12914)
GIVEN `the document is made available on a website` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the website is maintained by or on behalf of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the website identifies the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 926A(2) the first condition is met` MEANS
    IF `the document is made available on a website` AND `the website is maintained by or on behalf of the company` AND `the website identifies the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The first condition is that the document is made available on a website which— (a) is maintained by or on behalf of the company, and (b) identifies the company"

-- src:12915 | (3) The second condition is that access to the document on the website is not conditional on payment of a fee or otherwise restricted.
@ref s 926A(3) The second condition: access to the document is not conditional on a fee or otherwise restricted (src:12915)
GIVEN `access to the document on the website is conditional on payment of a fee or otherwise restricted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 926A(3) the second condition is met` MEANS
    IF NOT (`access to the document on the website is conditional on payment of a fee or otherwise restricted`) THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The second condition is that access to the document on the website is not conditional on payment of a fee or otherwise restricted"

-- src:12916 | (4) The third condition is that the document remains available on the website throughout the period beginning one month before, and ending on, the date of any meeting of the company summoned for the purpose of approving the scheme.
@ref s 926A(4) The third condition: the document remains available throughout the period (src:12916)
GIVEN `first day of continuous availability` IS A DATE
      `last day of continuous availability` IS A DATE
      `date of any meeting of the company summoned for the purpose of approving the scheme` IS A DATE
      `s 940A(1) the failure to make the document available throughout the period is to be disregarded` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 926A(4) the third condition is met` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 906A(6) the document was available throughout the period beginning one month before, and ending on, the date` `first day of continuous availability` `last day of continuous availability` `date of any meeting of the company summoned for the purpose of approving the scheme`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 940A(1) the failure to make the document available throughout the period is to be disregarded` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE -- s 940A: the failure "is to be disregarded"
        IF `s 940A(1) the failure to make the document available throughout the period is to be disregarded` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether section 940A disregards the failure is not known
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The third condition is that the document remains available on the website throughout the period beginning one month before, and ending on, the date of any meeting"

-- (6): where members can obtain copies only as mentioned in subsection (5), section 926(1)(a) applies even if the conditions are met.
-- JURAL the member: claim to inspect at the registered office (unless the website conditions are met) | the company: duty to allow inspection or to meet the conditions
-- src:12911 | (1) Section 926(1)(a) does not apply to a document if the conditions in subsections (2) to (4) are met in relation to that document. This is subject to subsection (6).
@ref s 926A(1) Section 911(1)(a) does not apply to a document if the conditions in subsections (2) to (4) are met, subject to subsection (6) (src:12911)
GIVEN `s 926A(2) the first condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 926A(3) the second condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 926A(4) the third condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 926A(6) members can obtain copies only as mentioned in subsection (5)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 926A(1) section 926(1)(a) does not apply to the document` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 926A(6) members can obtain copies only as mentioned in subsection (5)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where members of a company are able to obtain copies of a document only as mentioned in subsection (5), section 926(1)(a) applies to that document even if the conditions in subsections (2) to (4) are met"
        IF elem (JUST FALSE) (LIST `s 926A(2) the first condition is met`, `s 926A(3) the second condition is met`, `s 926A(4) the third condition is met`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Section 911(1)(a) does not apply to a document if the conditions in subsections (2) to (4) are met" (an unmet "if": marginal reading (a))
        IF elem NOTHING (LIST `s 926A(2) the first condition is met`, `s 926A(3) the second condition is met`, `s 926A(4) the third condition is met`, `s 926A(6) members can obtain copies only as mentioned in subsection (5)`)
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): an answer is not known and no condition has failed
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- JURAL the person: claim to a copy he can retain and print | the company: duty to keep the document on the website so that he can
-- src:12917 | (5) A person is able to obtain a copy of a document as required by section 926(1)(b) if—
-- src:12918 | (a) the conditions in subsections (2) and (3) are met in relation to that document, and
-- src:12919 | (b) the person is able, throughout the period specified in subsection (4)—
-- src:12920 | (i) i)to retain a copy of the document as made available on the website, and
-- src:12921 | (ii) to produce a hard copy of it.
@ref s 926A(5) A person is able to obtain a copy as section 926(1)(b) requires if the first two conditions are met and he can retain and print it (src:12917-12921)
GIVEN `s 926A(2) the first condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 926A(3) the second condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is able, throughout the period specified in subsection (4), to retain a copy of the document as made available on the website` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is able, throughout that period, to produce a hard copy of it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 926A(5) the person is able to obtain a copy as section 926(1)(b) requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 926A(2) the first condition is met` EQUALS JUST FALSE OR `s 926A(3) the second condition is met` EQUALS JUST FALSE
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is able to obtain a copy of a document as required by section 926(1)(b) if— (a) the conditions in subsections (2) and (3) are met" (an unmet "if": marginal reading (a))
        IF NOT (`the person is able, throughout the period specified in subsection (4), to retain a copy of the document as made available on the website` AND `the person is able, throughout that period, to produce a hard copy of it`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) the person is able, throughout the period specified in subsection (4)— (i) to retain a copy ..., and (ii) to produce a hard copy of it"
        IF `s 926A(2) the first condition is met` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `s 926A(3) the second condition is met` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a condition's answer is not known

-- src:12922 | (6) Where members of a company are able to obtain copies of a document only as mentioned in subsection (5), section 926(1)(a) applies to that document even if the conditions in subsections (2) to (4) are met.
@ref s 926A(6) Where copies can be obtained only as mentioned in subsection (5), section 926(1)(a) applies even if the conditions are met (src:12922)
