-- (instantiated from the twin block of Report on material changes of assets of merging companies (s 911B); see work/expand.py)
§§ `Report on material changes of assets of transferor company (division) (s 927)`

-- src:12924 | (1) The directors of the transferor company must report—
-- src:12925 | (a) to every meeting of the members, or any class of members, of that company summoned for the purpose of agreeing to the scheme, and
-- src:12926 | (b) to the directors of each existing transferee company,
-- src:12927 | any material changes in the property and liabilities of the transferor company between the date when the draft terms were adopted and the date of the meeting in question.
@ref s 927(1) The directors of each merging company must report material changes in property and liabilities to meetings and to the other companies' directors (src:12924-12927)
GIVEN `s 927(3) the requirement in section 927 is excluded` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the directors have reported to every meeting of the members, or any class of members, summoned to agree to the scheme any material changes in the property and liabilities of the transferor company between the date when the draft terms were adopted and the date of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors have reported those changes to the directors of each existing transferee company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 903(1) status of a requirement`
`s 927(1) the directors have reported material changes in property and liabilities` MEANS
    `s 903(1) the status of the requirement` `s 927(3) the requirement in section 927 is excluded`
        (`the directors have reported to every meeting of the members, or any class of members, summoned to agree to the scheme any material changes in the property and liabilities of the transferor company between the date when the draft terms were adopted and the date of the meeting` AND `the directors have reported those changes to the directors of each existing transferee company`)

-- src:12928 | (2) The directors of each existing transferee company must in turn—
-- src:12929 | (a) report those matters to every meeting of the members, or any class of members, of that company summoned for the purpose of agreeing to the scheme, or
-- src:12930 | (b) send a report of those matters to every member entitled to receive notice of such a meeting.
@ref s 927(2) The directors of each of each existing transferee company must in turn report those matters to the meeting or send a report to every member entitled to notice (src:12928-12930)
GIVEN `s 927(3) the requirement in section 927 is excluded` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the directors have reported those matters to every meeting of the members, or any class of members, summoned to agree to the scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors have sent a report of those matters to every member entitled to receive notice of such a meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 903(1) status of a requirement`
`s 927(2) the directors of each existing transferee company have reported those matters in turn` MEANS
    `s 903(1) the status of the requirement` `s 927(3) the requirement in section 927 is excluded`
        (`the directors have reported those matters to every meeting of the members, or any class of members, summoned to agree to the scheme` OR `the directors have sent a report of those matters to every member entitled to receive notice of such a meeting`)

-- src:12931 | (3) The requirement in this section is subject to section 933 (agreement to dispense with reports etc) and section 933A (certain requirements excluded where shareholders given proportional rights).
@ref s 927(3) The requirement is subject to sections 933 and 933A (src:12931)
GIVEN `s 933(1) the requirements are dispensed with by agreement` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 933A(2) the requirements of sections 923, 924, 925 and 927 do not apply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 927(3) the requirement in section 927 is excluded` MEANS
    `s 903(2) any of the provisions answers yes` (LIST `s 933(1) the requirements are dispensed with by agreement`, `s 933A(2) the requirements of sections 923, 924, 925 and 927 do not apply`)

§§ `Approval of articles of new transferee company (division) (s 928)`

-- JURAL the transferor company's members: right to approve the articles of each new transferee company by ordinary resolution | the directors: duty to put them to the members
-- src:12933 | (1) The articles of every new transferee company, or a draft of them, must be approved by ordinary resolution of the transferor company.
-- src:12934 | (2) Subsection (1) does not apply in the case of a compromise or arrangement to be sanctioned under Part 26A.
@ref s 928 The articles of every new transferee company, or a draft of them, must be approved by ordinary resolution of the transferor company (src:12933-12934)
GIVEN `the compromise or arrangement is to be sanctioned under Part 26A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 282 the resolution approving the articles or a draft of them is an ordinary resolution of the transferor company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 903(1) status of a requirement`
`s 928(1) the articles of every new transferee company have been approved by ordinary resolution of the transferor company` MEANS
    IF `the compromise or arrangement is to be sanctioned under Part 26A`
    THEN `s 903(1) requirement does not apply` -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply in the case of a compromise or arrangement to be sanctioned under Part 26A"
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 282 the resolution approving the articles or a draft of them is an ordinary resolution of the transferor company`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN `s 903(1) requirement complied with`
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN `s 903(1) requirement not complied with` -- a bare "must" not done (fork F3)
         WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 903(1) requirement not covered` -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): section 282 is outside this range

§§ `Protection of holders of securities to which special rights attached (division) (s 929)`

-- (instantiated from the twin block of Protection of holders of securities to which special rights attached (merger) (s 913); see work/expand.py)
§§ `Protection of holders of securities to which special rights attached (division) (s 929)`

-- JURAL the holder of the securities: claim to rights of equivalent value in a transferee company | the scheme (and a transferee company): duty to provide them
-- src:12936 | (1) The scheme must provide that where any securities of the transferor company (other than shares) to which special rights are attached are held by a person otherwise than as a member or creditor of the company, that person is to receive rights in a transferee company of equivalent value.
-- src:12937 | (2) Subsection (1) does not apply if—
-- src:12938 | (a) the holder has agreed otherwise, or
-- src:12939 | (b) the holder is, or under the scheme is to be, entitled to have the securities purchased by a transferee company on terms that the court considers reasonable.
@ref s 913 The scheme must provide that holders of securities (other than shares) with special rights receive rights of equivalent value (src:12936-12939)
GIVEN `securities of a transferor company (other than shares) to which special rights are attached are held by a person otherwise than as a member or creditor of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the holder has agreed otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the holder is, or under the scheme is to be, entitled to have the securities purchased by a transferee company on terms that the court considers reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the scheme provides that the holder is to receive rights in a transferee company of equivalent value` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 903(1) status of a requirement`
`s 929(1) the scheme protects the holder of securities to which special rights are attached` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`securities of a transferor company (other than shares) to which special rights are attached are held by a person otherwise than as a member or creditor of the company`)
            THEN `s 903(1) requirement does not apply` -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where any securities of a transferor company (other than shares) to which special rights are attached are held by a person otherwise than as a member or creditor"
        IF `the holder has agreed otherwise` OR `the holder is, or under the scheme is to be, entitled to have the securities purchased by a transferee company on terms that the court considers reasonable`
            THEN `s 903(1) requirement does not apply` -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply if— (a) the holder has agreed otherwise, or (b) the holder is, or under the scheme is to be, entitled to have the securities purchased"
        IF `the scheme provides that the holder is to receive rights in a transferee company of equivalent value`
            THEN `s 903(1) requirement complied with`
        OTHERWISE `s 903(1) requirement not complied with` -- a bare "must" not done (fork F3)

