GIVEN `the scheme provides for shares in a transferee company to be allotted to the transferor company (or its nominee) in respect of shares in the transferor company held by the transferor company itself (or its nominee)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the scheme provides for shares in a transferee company to be allotted to a transferee company (or its nominee) in respect of shares in the transferor company held by a transferee company (or its nominee)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 903(1) status of a requirement`
`s 930 the scheme does not provide for the allotment of shares the section forbids` MEANS
    IF `the scheme provides for shares in a transferee company to be allotted to the transferor company (or its nominee) in respect of shares in the transferor company held by the transferor company itself (or its nominee)`
       OR `the scheme provides for shares in a transferee company to be allotted to a transferee company (or its nominee) in respect of shares in the transferor company held by a transferee company (or its nominee)`
    THEN `s 903(1) requirement not complied with` -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The scheme must not provide for any shares in a transferee company to be allotted to"
    ELSE `s 903(1) requirement complied with`

