-- before the date of the first meeting of members of the transferor company summoned to agree to the scheme.
-- src:12949 | (3A) This subsection is satisfied if publication of notice of receipt of the draft terms by the registrar took place in respect of all the companies involved in the division at least one month before the date of the court's order.
@ref s 931(3A) Publication of notice of receipt of the draft terms took place at least one month before the first meeting of members of the transferor company (src:12949)
GIVEN `date the registrar published notice of receipt of the draft terms in respect of all the companies involved in the division` IS A DATE
      `date of the court's order` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 931(3A) subsection (3A) is satisfied` MEANS
    IF `s 906(3) the date one month before` `date of the court's order` AT LEAST `date the registrar published notice of receipt of the draft terms in respect of all the companies involved in the division`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This subsection is satisfied if publication of notice of receipt of the draft terms by the registrar took place in respect of all the companies involved in the division at least one month before the date of the first meeting"

-- src:12950 | (3B) This subsection is satisfied if—
-- src:12951 | (a) the conditions in section 921A(2) to (4) are met in respect of each of the companies involved in the division,
-- src:12952 | (b) in each case, the registrar published the notice mentioned in subsection (4) of that section in the Gazette at least one month before the date of the court's order, and
-- src:12953 | (c) the draft terms remained available on the website throughout the period beginning one month before, and ending on, that date.
@ref s 931(3B) The first condition, second way: the website route (src:12950-12953)
GIVEN `s 921A(2) the first condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 921A(3) the second condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 921A(4) the third condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `date the registrar published the notice mentioned in section 921A(4) in the Gazette` IS A DATE
      `date of the court's order` IS A DATE
      `first day on which the draft terms were continuously available on the website` IS A DATE
      `last day on which the draft terms were continuously available on the website` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 931(3B) subsection (3B) is satisfied` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF elem (JUST FALSE) (LIST `s 921A(2) the first condition is met`, `s 921A(3) the second condition is met`, `s 921A(4) the third condition is met`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) the conditions in section 906A(2) to (4) are met in respect of all the companies involved in the division" (an unmet "if": marginal reading (a))
        IF `s 906(3) the date one month before` `date of the court's order` LESS THAN `date the registrar published the notice mentioned in section 921A(4) in the Gazette`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) the registrar published the notice mentioned in subsection (4) of that section in the Gazette at least one month before the date of the first meeting"
        IF NOT (`s 906A(6) the document was available throughout the period beginning one month before, and ending on, the date` `first day on which the draft terms were continuously available on the website` `last day on which the draft terms were continuously available on the website` `date of the court's order`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) the draft terms remained available on the website throughout the period beginning one month before, and ending on, that date"
        IF elem NOTHING (LIST `s 921A(2) the first condition is met`, `s 921A(3) the second condition is met`, `s 921A(4) the third condition is met`)
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a condition's answer is not known and none has failed
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:12948 | (3) The first condition is that either subsection (3A) or subsection (3B) is satisfied.
@ref s 931(3) The first condition: subsection (3A) or subsection (3B) is satisfied (src:12948)
GIVEN `s 931(3A) subsection (3A) is satisfied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 931(3B) subsection (3B) is satisfied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 931(3) the first condition is met` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 903(2) any of the provisions answers yes` (LIST `s 931(3A) subsection (3A) is satisfied`, `s 931(3B) subsection (3B) is satisfied`) EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 903(2) any of the provisions answers yes` (LIST `s 931(3A) subsection (3A) is satisfied`, `s 931(3B) subsection (3B) is satisfied`) EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): an answer is not known and neither way is satisfied
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The first condition is that either subsection (3A) or subsection (3B) is satisfied"

-- (4A): the members of every company involved in the division were able, during the period beginning one month before and ending on the date mentioned in (3A), to inspect the document at the registered office.
-- src:12955 | (4A) This subsection is satisfied for a document if the members of every company involved in the division were able during the period beginning one month before, and ending on, the date of the court's order to inspect that document at the registered office of their company.
@ref s 931(4A) The members of every company involved in the division were able to inspect the document at its registered office throughout the period (src:12955)
GIVEN `first day on which the members of every company involved in the division were able to inspect the document at its registered office` IS A DATE
      `last day on which the members of every company involved in the division were able to inspect the document at its registered office` IS A DATE
      `date of the court's order` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 931(4A) subsection (4A) is satisfied for the document` MEANS
    IF `s 906A(6) the document was available throughout the period beginning one month before, and ending on, the date` `first day on which the members of every company involved in the division were able to inspect the document at its registered office` `last day on which the members of every company involved in the division were able to inspect the document at its registered office` `date of the court's order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This subsection is satisfied for a document if the members of every company involved in the division were able during the period beginning one month before, and ending on, the date mentioned in subsection (3A) to inspect that document at the registered office of that company"

-- src:12956 | (4B) This subsection is satisfied for a document if—
-- src:12957 | (a) the document is made available on a website which is maintained by or on behalf of the company to which it relates and identifies the company,
-- src:12958 | (b) access to the document on the website is not conditional on payment of a fee or otherwise restricted, and
-- src:12959 | (c) the document remains available on the website throughout the period beginning one month before, and ending on, the date of the court's order.
@ref s 931(4B) The document was on the transferee company's website, free of fee and restriction, throughout the period (src:12956-12959)
GIVEN `the document is made available on a website which is maintained by or on behalf of the transferee company and identifies the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `access to the document on the website is conditional on the payment of a fee or otherwise restricted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `first day on which the document was continuously available on the website` IS A DATE
      `last day on which the document was continuously available on the website` IS A DATE
      `date of the court's order` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 931(4B) subsection (4B) is satisfied for the document` MEANS
    IF `the document is made available on a website which is maintained by or on behalf of the transferee company and identifies the company`
       AND (NOT (`access to the document on the website is conditional on the payment of a fee or otherwise restricted`))
       AND `s 906A(6) the document was available throughout the period beginning one month before, and ending on, the date` `first day on which the document was continuously available on the website` `last day on which the document was continuously available on the website` `date of the court's order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This subsection is satisfied for a document if— (a) the document is made available on a website which is maintained by or on behalf of the transferee company and identifies the company, (b) access to the document on the website is not conditional on the payment of a fee or otherwise restricted, and (c) the document remains available on the website throughout the period"

-- The documents are those listed in the applicable paragraphs of section 926(3)(a) to (f): one answer per document (the caller supplies the answer of (4A) or (4B) for each).
-- src:12954 | (4) The second condition is that subsection (4A) or (4B) is satisfied for each of the documents listed in the applicable paragraphs of section 926(3) relating to every company involved in the division.
@ref s 931(4) The second condition: subsection (4A) or (4B) is satisfied for each of the documents listed in section 926(3)(a) to (f) (src:12954)
GIVEN `for each of the documents the answer of subsection (4A) or subsection (4B)` IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 931(4) the second condition is met` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF elem (JUST FALSE) `for each of the documents the answer of subsection (4A) or subsection (4B)`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The second condition is that subsection (4A) or (4B) is satisfied for each of the documents listed in the applicable paragraphs of section 926(3)(a) to (f)"
        IF elem NOTHING `for each of the documents the answer of subsection (4A) or subsection (4B)`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a document's answer is not known and none has failed
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:12960 | (4C) The third condition is that the members of every company involved in the division were able to obtain copies of the documents mentioned in subsection (4), or any part of those documents, on request and free of charge, throughout the period beginning one month before, and ending on, the date of the court's order.
@ref s 931(4C) The third condition: the members of every company involved in the division were able to obtain copies free of charge throughout the period (src:12960)
GIVEN `first day on which the members of every company involved in the division were able to obtain copies on request free of charge` IS A DATE
      `last day on which the members of every company involved in the division were able to obtain copies on request free of charge` IS A DATE
      `date of the court's order` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 931(4C) the third condition is met` MEANS
    IF `s 906A(6) the document was available throughout the period beginning one month before, and ending on, the date` `first day on which the members of every company involved in the division were able to obtain copies on request free of charge` `last day on which the members of every company involved in the division were able to obtain copies on request free of charge` `date of the court's order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The third condition is that the members of every company involved in the division were able to obtain copies of the documents ... on request and free of charge, throughout the period beginning one month before, and ending on, the date mentioned in subsection (3A)"

-- src:12961 | (4D) For the purposes of subsection (4C)—
-- src:12962 | (a) section 926A(5) applies as it applies for the purposes of section 926(1)(b), and
-- src:12963 | (b) Part 4 of Schedule 5 (communications by means of a website) does not apply.
@ref s 931(4D) For the purposes of subsection (4C), section 926A(5) applies and Part 4 of Schedule 5 does not (src:12961-12963)
GIVEN `the purposes are those of subsection (4C)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 931(4D) section 926A(5) applies and Part 4 of Schedule 5 does not apply` MEANS
    IF `the purposes are those of subsection (4C)` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purposes of subsection (4C)"


-- "it is not necessary for the scheme to be approved at a meeting ... if the court is satisfied that the following conditions have been complied with":
-- the court's satisfaction is a conditional input (fork F4); the four conditions are functions of the facts.
-- JURAL the members of every company involved in the division: immunity from being called to a meeting | the court: power to excuse the meeting on being satisfied
-- src:12947 | (2) It is not necessary for the scheme to be approved by a meeting of the members, or any class of members, of the transferor company if the court is satisfied that the following conditions have been complied with.
@ref s 931(2) It is not necessary for the scheme to be approved at a meeting of the members of every company involved in the division if the court is satisfied that the conditions have been complied with (src:12947)
GIVEN `s 931(1) this section applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 931(3) the first condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 931(4) the second condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 931(4C) the third condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 931(6) the fourth condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the following conditions have been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 931(2) the meeting of members of the transferor company is not required` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 931(1) this section applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies in the case of a division where"
        IF NOT (`the court is satisfied that the following conditions have been complied with`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the court is satisfied that the following conditions have been complied with" (an unmet "if": marginal reading (a))
        IF elem (JUST FALSE) (LIST `s 931(3) the first condition is met`, `s 931(4) the second condition is met`, `s 931(4C) the third condition is met`, `s 931(6) the fourth condition is met`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the following conditions have been complied with" (a condition is not met)
        IF `s 931(1) this section applies` EQUALS NOTHING OR elem NOTHING (LIST `s 931(3) the first condition is met`, `s 931(4) the second condition is met`, `s 931(4C) the third condition is met`, `s 931(6) the fourth condition is met`)
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): an answer is not known and none has failed
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- The fourth condition: the directors of the transferor company have sent a report of any material change between the date the terms were adopted and the date one month before the court's order.
-- JURAL the members and the directors of the existing transferee companies: claim to a report of material change | the directors of the transferor company: duty to send it
-- src:12965 | (6) The fourth condition is that the directors of the transferor company have sent—
-- src:12966 | (a) to every member who would have been entitled to receive notice of a meeting to agree to the scheme (had any such meeting been called), and
-- src:12967 | (b) to the directors of every existing transferee company,
-- src:12968 | a report of any material change in the property and liabilities of the transferor company between the date when the terms were adopted by the directors and the date one month before the date of the court's order.
@ref s 931(6) The fourth condition: the directors of the transferor company have sent a report of any material change in property and liabilities (src:12965-12968)
GIVEN `the directors of the transferor company have sent a report to every member who would have been entitled to receive notice of a meeting to agree to the scheme (had any such meeting been called)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors of the transferor company have sent a report to the directors of every existing transferee company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date up to which the report states any material change in the property and liabilities of the transferor company` IS A DATE
      `date of the court's order` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 931(6) the fourth condition is met` MEANS
    IF `the directors of the transferor company have sent a report to every member who would have been entitled to receive notice of a meeting to agree to the scheme (had any such meeting been called)`
       AND `the directors of the transferor company have sent a report to the directors of every existing transferee company`
       AND `the date up to which the report states any material change in the property and liabilities of the transferor company` AT LEAST (`s 906(3) the date one month before` `date of the court's order`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The fourth condition is that the directors of the transferor company have sent— (a) to every member ..., and (b) to the directors of every existing transferee company, a report of any material change ... between the date when the terms were adopted by the directors and the date one month before the date of the court's order"

-- src:12964 | (5) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- s 931(5): the text shows only dots (repealed or omitted). Coverage row: repealed or blank in this text. No L4.

§§ `Other circumstances in which meeting of members of transferor company not required (division) (s 931A)`

-- JURAL the members of the transferor company: immunity from being called to a meeting | whoever proposes the scheme: no duty to put it to them
-- src:12971 | In the case of a compromise or arrangement to be sanctioned under Part 26A, it is not necessary for the scheme to be approved by the members of the transferor company.
@ref s 931A In the case of a compromise or arrangement to be sanctioned under Part 26A, it is not necessary for the scheme to be approved by the members of the transferor company (src:12971)
GIVEN `the compromise or arrangement is to be sanctioned under Part 26A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 931A(1) the meeting of members of the transferor company is not required` MEANS
    IF `the compromise or arrangement is to be sanctioned under Part 26A` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In the case of a compromise or arrangement to be sanctioned under Part 26A, it is not necessary" (an unmet "in the case of": the 2026-11-05 "where" ruling)

§§ `Circumstances in which meeting of members of transferee company not required (division) (s 932)`

-- (instantiated from the twin block of Circumstances in which meeting of members of transferee company not required (merger) (s 916); see work/expand.py)
§§ `Circumstances in which meeting of members of transferee company not required (division) (s 932)`


-- The first condition, first way (3A): the registrar published notice of receipt of the draft terms in respect of the transferee company at least one month
-- before the date of the first meeting of members of the transferor company summoned to agree to the scheme.
-- src:12975 | (2A) This subsection is satisfied if publication of notice of receipt of the draft terms by the registrar took place in respect of the transferee company at least one month before the date of the first meeting of members of the transferor company summoned for the purposes of agreeing to the scheme.
@ref s 932(2A) Publication of notice of receipt of the draft terms took place at least one month before the first meeting of members of the transferor company (src:12975)
GIVEN `date the registrar published notice of receipt of the draft terms in respect of the transferee company` IS A DATE
      `date of the first meeting of members, or any class of members, of the transferor company summoned for the purpose of agreeing to the scheme` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 932(2A) subsection (2A) is satisfied` MEANS
    IF `s 906(3) the date one month before` `date of the first meeting of members, or any class of members, of the transferor company summoned for the purpose of agreeing to the scheme` AT LEAST `date the registrar published notice of receipt of the draft terms in respect of the transferee company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This subsection is satisfied if publication of notice of receipt of the draft terms by the registrar took place in respect of the transferee company at least one month before the date of the first meeting"

-- src:12976 | (2B) This subsection is satisfied if—
-- src:12977 | (a) the conditions in section 921A(2) to (4) are met in respect of the transferee company,
-- src:12978 | (b) the registrar published the notice mentioned in subsection (4) of that section in the Gazette at least one month before the date of the first meeting of members of the transferor company summoned for the purposes of agreeing to the scheme, and
-- src:12979 | (c) the draft terms remained available on the website throughout the period beginning one month before, and ending on, that date.
@ref s 932(2B) The first condition, second way: the website route (src:12976-12979)
GIVEN `s 921A(2) the first condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 921A(3) the second condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 921A(4) the third condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `date the registrar published the notice mentioned in section 921A(4) in the Gazette` IS A DATE
      `date of the first meeting of members, or any class of members, of the transferor company summoned for the purpose of agreeing to the scheme` IS A DATE
      `first day on which the draft terms were continuously available on the website` IS A DATE
      `last day on which the draft terms were continuously available on the website` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 932(2B) subsection (2B) is satisfied` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF elem (JUST FALSE) (LIST `s 921A(2) the first condition is met`, `s 921A(3) the second condition is met`, `s 921A(4) the third condition is met`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) the conditions in section 906A(2) to (4) are met in respect of the transferee company" (an unmet "if": marginal reading (a))
        IF `s 906(3) the date one month before` `date of the first meeting of members, or any class of members, of the transferor company summoned for the purpose of agreeing to the scheme` LESS THAN `date the registrar published the notice mentioned in section 921A(4) in the Gazette`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) the registrar published the notice mentioned in subsection (3) of that section in the Gazette at least one month before the date of the first meeting"
        IF NOT (`s 906A(6) the document was available throughout the period beginning one month before, and ending on, the date` `first day on which the draft terms were continuously available on the website` `last day on which the draft terms were continuously available on the website` `date of the first meeting of members, or any class of members, of the transferor company summoned for the purpose of agreeing to the scheme`)
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) the draft terms remained available on the website throughout the period beginning one month before, and ending on, that date"
        IF elem NOTHING (LIST `s 921A(2) the first condition is met`, `s 921A(3) the second condition is met`, `s 921A(4) the third condition is met`)
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a condition's answer is not known and none has failed
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:12974 | (2) The first condition is that either subsection (2A) or subsection (2B) is satisfied.
@ref s 932(2) The first condition: subsection (2A) or subsection (2B) is satisfied (src:12974)
GIVEN `s 932(2A) subsection (2A) is satisfied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 932(2B) subsection (2B) is satisfied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 932(2) the first condition is met` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 903(2) any of the provisions answers yes` (LIST `s 932(2A) subsection (2A) is satisfied`, `s 932(2B) subsection (2B) is satisfied`) EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 903(2) any of the provisions answers yes` (LIST `s 932(2A) subsection (2A) is satisfied`, `s 932(2B) subsection (2B) is satisfied`) EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): an answer is not known and neither way is satisfied
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The first condition is that either subsection (2A) or subsection (2B) is satisfied"

